//! Oracle 8 (docs/testing.md): our booleans against those of an
//! independent kernel.
//!
//! `tests/fixtures/boolean_corpus.json` holds some two thousand pairs of
//! primitive solids, in the configurations a boolean has to get right, with
//! what FreeCAD measured for their common, cut and fuse. It is generated by
//! `cargo xtask boolean-corpus` (which needs FreeCAD; this test does not)
//! and pinned in the repository. Here every pair is built with
//! `kernel::primitives`, the three booleans are run, and volume, area,
//! centroid and the number of shells are compared with the reference.
//!
//! Per case and operation the outcome is one of:
//!
//! - `match`: agrees with a reference graded `exact`;
//! - `match~`: agrees with a reference graded `approximate`, within the
//!   wider bound that reference deserves (see [`Bounds`]);
//! - `empty`: we say the result is empty and the reference has no volume;
//! - `unsupported`: the kernel refuses, with its reason;
//! - `unscored`: FreeCAD's own answer is `unreliable` (it failed, called
//!   its result invalid, or contradicts itself, a count of sampled points,
//!   or the construction of the case), so there is nothing to compare with;
//!   our result must still be a valid body;
//! - `MISMATCH`: we return a body that disagrees with the reference, or an
//!   empty result where the reference has volume. The test fails;
//! - `INVALID`: a panic, a body that fails the checker, an error that is
//!   neither a refusal nor an empty result, or an operand whose mass
//!   properties differ from FreeCAD's. The test fails.
//!
//! The test also holds a floor: the number of agreeing outcomes (`match`,
//! `match~`, `empty`) may not go down ([`AGREEING_FLOOR`]).
//!
//! Run one case or one category, with every number printed:
//!
//! ```sh
//! BOOLEAN_CORPUS_CASE=flush/block-cylinder/003 \
//!     cargo test -p craft3d-kernel --test boolean_corpus -- --nocapture
//! BOOLEAN_CORPUS_CATEGORY=tangent cargo test -p craft3d-kernel --test boolean_corpus
//! BOOLEAN_CORPUS_VERBOSE=1 BOOLEAN_CORPUS_CATEGORY=near cargo test ... # every case printed
//! ```
//!
//! The score table goes to `target/evidence/booleans/corpus-score.txt`.

#![allow(
    clippy::unwrap_used,
    clippy::expect_used,
    clippy::panic,
    clippy::indexing_slicing
)]

